"""UOS Library AI - library_academic_faq.py

80 Academic & Research Assistance FAQs in 8 categories of 10:
assignment assistance, research topic selection, literature review,
research methodology, referencing & citation, research tools &
software, thesis & academic writing, and plagiarism & research
ethics.

IMPORTANT - two kinds of content, kept clearly separate by the
"status" field of every entry:

  * "official UOS information" - a claim about a service that the
    Wazir Agha Library actually offers, taken from the official
    pages already used by this project (Information Services page
    and Research Support Lab page, read in full on 23 Nov 2026).
  * "general academic guidance" - ordinary study/research guidance
    of the kind taught in research-methods courses everywhere. It is
    NOT a UOS service, policy or rule, and answers are worded that
    way.

Accuracy rules:
  * No invented research papers, citations, references, statistics
    or Turnitin results. Referencing formats are shown as TEMPLATES
    with placeholders, never as fake real references.
  * No universal numbers are invented: source counts for a review,
    sample sizes, thesis length and "acceptable" similarity
    percentages depend on the department/supervisor - the FAQs say
    so. The UOS Turnitin threshold is not published in the sources
    checked (see also library_services_faq.py FS53).
  * The library will not write a student's assignment or thesis;
    its role is training, searching assistance and resources.

Matching uses the same strict design as library_services_faq.py
(distinctive phrases + canonical-question containment scaled by
matched words, with a user-coverage guard and a number-token guard;
ties return None). This module is checked in app.py AFTER the rules
and services FAQs, so official rules/services answers keep priority.
"""

